For projectile motion,
$\begin{aligned}
& \theta=\tan ^{-1}(\sqrt{7}) \Rightarrow \tan \theta=\sqrt{7} \\
& \text{ At } y=\frac{H}{2}, v_y^2=u_y^2-2 g\left(\frac{H}{2}\right) \\
& \therefore \quad v_y^2=u^2 \sin ^2 \theta-g H, v_x^2=u_x^2=u^2 \cos ^2 \theta \\
& \therefore \quad v=\sqrt{v_x^2+v_y^2}=\sqrt{u^2\left(\sin ^2 \theta+\cos ^2 \theta\right)-g H} \\
& =\sqrt{u^2-\mathrm{gH}}
\end{aligned}$Also, $v=\mathrm{nu} \Rightarrow \mathrm{v}^2=\mathrm{n}^2 \mathrm{u}^2\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \mathrm{u}^2-\mathrm{gH}=\mathrm{n}^2 \mathrm{u}^2 \\
& \Rightarrow \mathrm{n}^2=1-\frac{\mathrm{gH}}{\mathrm{u}^2}=1-\frac{\frac{\mathrm{u}^2 \sin ^2 \theta}{2}}{\mathrm{u}^2}=1-\frac{1}{2}\left(1-\frac{1}{1+\tan ^2 \theta}\right) \\
& =1-\frac{1}{2}\left(1-\frac{1}{1+7}\right)=\frac{9}{16} \therefore \mathrm{n}=\frac{3}{4}
\end{aligned}$

